node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# pnpm's content-addressed install cache when a build runs inside the tree;
# it is a local artifact, never source (A16: 6,955 files / 125 MB leaked into
# the relay branch and had to be rewritten out).
.pnpm-store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source resolution, not version control. Tailwind decides which files can hold
# class names with gitignore semantics, and a DEEPER .gitignore's `!` patterns
# override a shallower file's. uv writes an ALLOW-LIST .gitignore — the single
# line `*` — at the root of every venv it creates and of every tool generation
# it installs, so in an installed tree (site-packages, or a `lop-update`
# generation under ~/.local/share/uv/tools or /var/folders) the whole web tree
# sits under a `*` and is invisible to the scanner: `pnpm build` then emits a
# stylesheet with no utilities, EXITS 0 (measured: 31 kB against 50 kB for
# these sources), and the phone renders unstyled with nothing in any log to
# say why. Upstream: tailwindlabs/tailwindcss#19844, #15452.
#
# So this file ships via package-data — an installed tree has no .gitignore of
# its own otherwise — and its `!` lines re-include the paths the build scans
# (the `@source` globs in src/styles/index.css). `!src/**` is what the scanner
# honours; `!src/**/*.ts` was measured and does not re-include on its own.
#
# Only `!src/**` is broad enough to touch a git rule, so `*.tsbuildinfo` is
# re-imposed below it (last match wins): the tsc build cache under src/ stays
# out of git exactly as it was. Do not "tidy" these lines away — the failure
# they prevent is a silent one.
!index.html
!scripts/
!src/
!src/**
*.tsbuildinfo
